meta {
  name: Assign Row (Cannot Sell)
  type: http
  seq: 29
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/carrier-reconciliation/runs/{{reconRunId}}/rows/{{reconAssignRowId}}/assignment
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{reconToken}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "userId": "{{reconCsrId}}"
  }
}

script:pre-request {
  // `Get Options` found no CSR who cannot book a sale — an agency that lets
  // its CSRs sell has nobody to refuse.
  if (!bru.getVar("reconCsrId")) bru.runner.skipRequest();
}

tests {
  test("returns 400 Bad Request", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(400);
  });

  test("because a row missing from the app needs someone who can book a sale", function () {
    expect(res.getBody().code).to.equal("RECONCILIATION_ASSIGNEE_CANNOT_SELL");
  });
}

docs {
  # PATCH …/assignment — a row missing from the app, to a CSR (400)

  The fixture's `900299990` is missing from the app, so whoever takes it
  records it as Sold or a Cancel rewrite by entering the lead and the sale —
  which needs `leads:write` **and** `deal_audits:write`. The demo's CSRs hold
  the CSR template, which has no `deal_audits:write` (`canRecordSale: false`
  on `Get Options`), so the row cannot go to them (owner, 28 Oct 2026).

  Checked by effective permission, never by role: a CSR the agency granted
  `deal_audits:write` qualifies. Only a **new** assignee is checked — a note
  change for the person who has the row is not. The same CSR can still be
  given a row in any other tab, which only ever takes Other.

  Skipped when `Get Options` found no such CSR (`reconCsrId` unset).

  ```json
  { "code": "RECONCILIATION_ASSIGNEE_CANNOT_SELL",
    "message": "A Dash sale missing from the app can be given only to someone who can book a sale (create leads and record sales)." }
  ```
}
